  <section class="section">
    <h2>What it's for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Is anything happening on the sun right now?</strong> One glance: a condition word, one honest sentence, and the numbers that back it up.</li>
      <li><strong>Will I see the aurora tonight?</strong> A forecast for your sky: your darkness window, moonlight, and NOAA's aurora map with your dot on it.</li>
      <li><strong>What does Kp 5 actually mean?</strong> Every number teaches itself — tap any card for a plain-English explanation with diagrams.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Features</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>The actual sun</strong> — live imagery from NASA's Solar Dynamics Observatory as the app's backdrop</li>
      <li><strong>Current conditions</strong> — geomagnetic activity, solar wind, flares, and radiation, composed from NOAA data</li>
      <li><strong>Aurora for your sky</strong> — local darkness, CME arrival forecasts, and the OVATION map with a viewline</li>
      <li><strong>Learn as you go</strong> — the Kp ladder, Bz explained, flare classes, NOAA scales, a glossary, and Sun &amp; Earth geometry made visual</li>
      <li><strong>Built like a weather app</strong> — scrubbable charts, a pixel sun with tappable active regions, honest offline behavior</li>
      <li><strong>Private by design</strong> — no servers, no accounts, no analytics. Your location never leaves your device.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>Helio collects nothing. It reads public NOAA and NASA feeds directly, and location is optional and processed on your device. Read the full <a href="/helio/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <p class="post-meta">Data: NOAA Space Weather Prediction Center and NASA (SDO, DONKI) · Built with SwiftUI, Swift Charts, and MapKit · by <a href="/about/">Dominic Critchlow</a></p>
  </section>
